---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import clients from '../data/clients.json';
---

<Layout title="SDub Media | Nashville Video Production">

<section class="hero">
  <span class="eyebrow">SDub Media &nbsp;·&nbsp; Nashville, TN</span>
  <h1><span class="accent">Recurring video</span> for Nashville businesses.</h1>
  <p class="hero-subtitle">A team of five. You sit down with us for a couple of hours and we turn it into a quarter of content. We also archive conferences, film dance recitals, and take a few weddings a year.</p>
  <div class="hero-ctas">
    <a href="/business" class="btn btn-primary">For Businesses</a>
    <a href="/weddings" class="btn">For Weddings</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Trusted by</span>
      {/* Was "Clients who show up every month". Untrue, since some of these
          were one-off projects rather than recurring work. This wording claims
          nothing about frequency and still describes the actual mix. The
          recurring-work pitch lives on /business, where it is accurate. */}
      <h2>Nashville businesses, schools, and arts organizations</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="logo-strip">
      {clients.map(c => (
        c.logo
          ? <img class="brand-logo-img" src={c.logo} alt={c.name} loading="lazy" />
          : <span class="brand">{c.name}</span>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{/* This replaced two separate sections that both used the eyebrow "What we do":
    a two-door Business/Weddings split and a two-tile services row. Neither
    mentioned /dance or /corporate-events, so half the site was invisible from
    the homepage. One section now covers all four, ordered by where the business
    is going: commercial work first, weddings last and deliberately smaller.

    The AI-generated images that were here originally were removed (generated
    stock is the worst possible tell for a video company). Every card carries a
    real frame. */}
<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What we do</span>
      {/* Said "Four kinds of work" over three cards, and neither of the two
          missing services had a door here at all. Real estate in particular is
          the sharpest offer on the site (a published price and a 48-hour
          turnaround) and the homepage was hiding it behind the nav. Five cards
          now, one per service page. Keep this count honest if a service is
          ever added or dropped. */}
      <h2>Five kinds of work, one way of working.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles tiles--five">
      <a href="/business" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/corporate/bts-bar-shoot.jpg" alt="A brand shoot in progress with two softboxes and two cameras set up around a bar" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1200" />
        <h3>Business</h3>
        <p>Interview-led content series, on-camera reels, headshot days, and brand films. You sit down for a couple of hours; we cut it into a quarter's worth of content. One broker's session with his top agents became nineteen pieces.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">What we do for businesses →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/corporate-events" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/corporate-events/camera-in-room.jpg" alt="A cinema camera at the back of a full conference room, speaker on stage beyond" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1200" />
        <h3>Corporate Events</h3>
        <p>Conference and speaker coverage. Every main-stage talk archived with board audio and your own slides, plus one highlight reel you can put to work while the event is still fresh.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">How event coverage works →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/dance" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/dance/jazz-group.jpg" alt="A jazz group posed on stage in green fringe costumes" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1069" />
        <h3>Dance</h3>
        <p>Recital films, studio promos, and season-long social content for studios around Nashville. The full show for families, the short cut for your website. We have done this for Elite Dance and Nolensville Dance Company.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">See the dance work →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/real-estate-photography" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/real-estate/living-room.jpg" alt="A bright living room photographed for a property listing" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1067" />
        <h3>Real Estate</h3>
        <p>Listing photos, video and drone work, priced per listing rather than per hour. Your gallery comes back in 48 hours, because a listing that goes live on Thursday cannot wait until the following week.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">See listing pricing →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/weddings" class="tile" style="color: inherit;">
        <img class="tile-image" src="/images/weddings/reception-dusk.jpg" alt="A beachside wedding reception under string lights after sunset" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900" />
        <h3>Weddings</h3>
        <p>A handful a year, all day, with pricing published on the page so you can rule us in or out before you email. A full film and a sizzle reel, plus family and senior portraits.</p>
        <span class="door-arrow">See wedding pricing →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-alt">
  <div class="container-narrow text-center">
    <span class="eyebrow">The difference</span>
    <h2 style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">Great content isn't a moment.<br>It's a system.</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-dim);">One video won't change your business. Fifty will. We design production systems that run month after month, same quality and same schedule, working alongside whoever owns marketing on your side. Your brand stays visible without anyone on your team running a production department.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/business" class="btn">See how it works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container-narrow text-center">
    <span class="eyebrow">Start a project</span>
    <h2>Let's talk about what you're planning.</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 520px; margin: 1.5rem auto 2rem;">A weekly series, a conference, a listing, a recital, or a wedding day. Start with a message and we'll reply within 24 hours.</p>
    <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start a conversation</a>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
